From: Ethan Zou <gloridust@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: set the NGD register base before
 adding its device

of_qcom_slim_ngd_register() fills in ngd->base only after
platform_device_add(). Adding the device probes it, and the probe can
already queue ngd_up_work; when the worker runs first it reads
NGD_STATUS from a NULL base:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000004
  Workqueue: events qcom_slim_ngd_up_worker [slim_qcom_ngd_ctrl]
  pc : qcom_slim_ngd_runtime_resume+0xb0/0x198 [slim_qcom_ngd_ctrl]

Seen on a Xiaomi Mi 5 (MSM8996) at boot; the worker then hangs and
takes the rest of the system with it. Compute the base first.
---
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1550,6 +1550,12 @@
 			return ret;
 		}
 		ngd->pdev->dev.of_node = node;
+		/*
+		 * Set up the registers before adding the device: probing it can
+		 * already queue ngd_up_work, which reads them.
+		 */
+		ngd->base = ctrl->base + ngd->id * data->offset +
+					(ngd->id - 1) * data->size;
 		ctrl->ngd = ngd;
 
 		ret = platform_device_add(ngd->pdev);
@@ -1559,8 +1565,6 @@
 			of_node_put(node);
 			return ret;
 		}
-		ngd->base = ctrl->base + ngd->id * data->offset +
-					(ngd->id - 1) * data->size;
 
 		return 0;
 	}
